WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Our heroes are continuing their journey to Lumiose City without Clemont,

2
00:00:05.666 --> 00:00:09.566
who is already there to prepare for his Gym Battle with Ash.

3
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:12.100
I hope Clemont will be OK by himself.

4
00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:13.566
Don't worry about him.

5
00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:17.033
I'll bet right now he's busy getting ready for Ash's Gym Battle.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.166
For sure.

7
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:23.433
- Mag...
- Bunn!

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.000
-Magneton is unable to battle.

9
00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:27.933
So that means you are the winner, sir.

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.433
That's wonderful. You finally learned it, Bunnelby.

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.766
Congratulations, sir.

12
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.666
Are you all right, Magneton?

13
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:37.266
Magneton.

14
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:41.433
Your preparations for battling Ash's Pikachu are proceeding quite smoothly.

15
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.666
True, but the real Ash is more, uh, dynamic.

16
00:00:45.733 --> 00:00:48.666
I've got the image of our battle in my mind, but...

17
00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:52.966
Of course! Say, Clembot, if I could digitise Ash's unique battle style

18
00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:56.400
and then input it into you, my training would be all the more realistic.

19
00:00:56.466 --> 00:00:58.100
A most excellent idea.

20
00:00:58.166 --> 00:01:00.833
I'll make all the preparations right away.

21
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.666
Winning a badge from this gym is going to be harder than Ash thinks.

22
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:08.066
We've gotta get ready for our battle too.

23
00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.900
Pumpkaboo, Shadow Ball! -Huh?

24
00:01:10.966 --> 00:01:12.600
Pika! Pi.

25
00:01:12.666 --> 00:01:15.333
Today's the day we catch Pikachu for sure.

26
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.933
- Team Rocket!
- Wobbuffet!

27
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

28
00:01:20.866 --> 00:01:22.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

29
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:26.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

30
00:01:26.066 --> 00:01:27.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

31
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:31.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

32
00:01:31.366 --> 00:01:34.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

33
00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:38.000
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

34
00:01:38.066 --> 00:01:41.966
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

35
00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:46.666
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

36
00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:48.933
♪ Pokémon! ♪

37
00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:56.533
A Fork in the Road! A Parting of the Ways!

38
00:01:59.266 --> 00:02:02.433
- Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

39
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.000
Already?

40
00:02:07.066 --> 00:02:09.466
Wobbuffet!

41
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.533
Man.

42
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.233
They made quicker work of us than usual, didn't they, Jessie?

43
00:02:29.633 --> 00:02:33.566
No! It's broken!

44
00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:35.633
-Wob! Wob, wob!

45
00:02:39.433 --> 00:02:43.300
Change of plan, Wobbuffet. Come on. Let's find the others.

46
00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:45.233
Wob! Wob, wob!

47
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.000
- James? Meowth? Pumpkaboo?
- Wobba! Wobbuffet!

48
00:02:51.366 --> 00:02:53.433
Uh, where are we?

49
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.866
Argh, I'm tired and I'm hungry too.

50
00:02:56.933 --> 00:02:58.933
Wobbuffet, do something right now!

51
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.866
Wob. Wobba. Wob?

52
00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:03.266
- What? Huh?
- Gloom.

53
00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:05.133
Ugh, stinky.

54
00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.533
Shoo! You smell like your freshness date's expired!

55
00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:12.600
-Wobba!

56
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.333
Wake up! Are you all right? Say something!

57
00:03:29.966 --> 00:03:32.700
You're OK. I'm so very relieved.

58
00:03:32.766 --> 00:03:36.733
- And your Wobbuffet's OK as well.
- Wobbuffet.

59
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.233
My name is White. I'm a doctor, so you don't have to worry about a thing.

60
00:03:42.966 --> 00:03:45.000
- Let's see.
- Huh?

61
00:03:45.066 --> 00:03:49.000
It looks like you were hit by a Stun Spore as well.

62
00:03:49.066 --> 00:03:51.000
Eat these berries.

63
00:03:51.066 --> 00:03:53.166
Huh? But...

64
00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:57.133
- Ah...
- Ah...

65
00:03:58.233 --> 00:04:02.233
I'm cured! Oh!

66
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.033
- So what's your name?
- Me? I'm Jessileah.

67
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.766
You'll catch a cold in those wet clothes of yours.

68
00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:12.366
My clinic's not very far from here. Come on, we can get you changed.

69
00:04:12.433 --> 00:04:13.966
- Thanks.
- Follow me.

70
00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:16.399
Um... Coming!

71
00:04:22.966 --> 00:04:26.766
- This probably doesn't suit me.
- No, you look just fine.

72
00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.866
You mean it?

73
00:04:30.966 --> 00:04:34.766
Wobba-ba!

74
00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:42.400
- You've got quite a garden out there.
- I planted each and every one.

75
00:04:42.466 --> 00:04:44.200
Since I'm the only doctor in town,

76
00:04:44.266 --> 00:04:48.233
it's up to me to grow all the healing herbs and berries I use in my practice.

77
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.233
Huh.

78
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:53.666
But I am an amateur when it comes to botany, although I do the best that I can.

79
00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.466
Hey there, doc, brought some fertiliser.

80
00:04:58.533 --> 00:05:02.033
Thank you. As always, you're a big help.

81
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.366
Well, the very least I can do is lend you a helpin' hand.

82
00:05:05.433 --> 00:05:08.800
Don't forget how you healed my Diggersby back when it got sick.

83
00:05:08.866 --> 00:05:11.366
- How are you feeling now?
- Diggersby.

84
00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:15.000
It's feelin' right as rain as you can see. Well, see you later!

85
00:05:15.066 --> 00:05:16.766
Thanks again for all your help.

86
00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.766
Now, take good care!

87
00:05:19.833 --> 00:05:22.933
- Well, guess I should be off.
- Off to where?

88
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.266
My daily rounds.

89
00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:25.566
- Um...
- Hm?

90
00:05:25.633 --> 00:05:27.600
Since you were kind enough to rescue me,

91
00:05:27.666 --> 00:05:30.600
would it be all right if I came along and gave you a hand?

92
00:05:30.666 --> 00:05:33.200
That would make my day.

93
00:05:36.966 --> 00:05:39.566
- Say ahh...
- Ahh...

94
00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.466
How's Bidoof?

95
00:05:41.533 --> 00:05:45.466
Its teeth seem to be just fine, but its gums aren't all that good.

96
00:05:45.533 --> 00:05:47.033
So what happened?

97
00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.300
Some lousy Pokémon hunter left a trap out here and poor Bidoof got caught in it.

98
00:05:51.366 --> 00:05:54.200
- A Pokémon hunter?
- Hm? Who are you?

99
00:05:54.266 --> 00:05:57.333
My name's Jessileah and I'm the doctor's assistant.

100
00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.433
This is my old friend, Beatrice.

101
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:03.533
- Assistant? Wow!
- Um, so what happened next?

102
00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.766
You see, that awful cage was made out of solid steel,

103
00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.766
but Bidoof used its powerful teeth to bite through the bars!

104
00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:12.766
Well then, that explains why its gums are so inflamed.

105
00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:16.766
If I ever find that mean Pokémon hunter, we'll have some settling up to do!

106
00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:20.533
Hold on. You'd better leave that sort of thing to Officer Jenny.

107
00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.500
Do you have any idea how long it would take Officer Jenny

108
00:06:23.566 --> 00:06:26.766
- to get all the way out here?
- That's no excuse for you to act up!

109
00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:27.766
No lectures!

110
00:06:27.833 --> 00:06:31.000
At least I'm not some mealy-mouthed frightened weakling like you!

111
00:06:31.066 --> 00:06:32.500
Uh, calm down.

112
00:06:32.566 --> 00:06:35.300
Don't go sticking your nose into dangerous business.

113
00:06:35.366 --> 00:06:37.500
You're not a child any more.

114
00:06:37.566 --> 00:06:39.500
I think we'd better get going. -Oh.

115
00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:41.866
Coming!

116
00:06:41.933 --> 00:06:46.633
This grown-up isn't afraid of anything, so have yourself a nice day!

117
00:06:51.566 --> 00:06:53.333
It's coming your way!

118
00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:56.333
Right! I've got it!

119
00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.300
There! Gotcha!

120
00:06:59.433 --> 00:07:00.733
- Ski-i-i-i!
- Uh!

121
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.933
That was amazing!

122
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.433
- OK, hang on while I do an examination.
- Right!

123
00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.166
Oh! You are a tough one, aren't you?

124
00:07:09.233 --> 00:07:11.933
Thanks! I guess I am really something special.

125
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.933
I have to tell you, a strong and capable woman like you

126
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.433
would make Dr White a perfect partner and a wonderful wife.

127
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.900
Oh! Me? A wife?

128
00:07:20.966 --> 00:07:23.600
Well, it would be the exact opposite

129
00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:27.000
of the glamorous life of a celebrity I've always dreamed of,

130
00:07:27.066 --> 00:07:28.833
but it would be so peaceful.

131
00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:31.633
I do think we could be happy together.

132
00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.100
Oh, go on!

133
00:07:33.166 --> 00:07:35.633
You really know how to embarrass a girl, don't you?

134
00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.433
- You're hurtin' my shoulder. Stop.
- Huh?

135
00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:43.166
I think that Skiddo was so out of control due to the effects of Poison Powder.

136
00:07:43.233 --> 00:07:45.933
It'll be just fine if it eats this Pecha Berry.

137
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.166
Oh, Doctor, thank you so much.

138
00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:50.566
- Here.
- Ski-i-i-i.

139
00:07:50.633 --> 00:07:52.500
Mm! Mm!

140
00:07:52.566 --> 00:07:54.800
Wow, I couldn't eat another bite.

141
00:07:54.866 --> 00:07:57.266
But we have macarons for dessert.

142
00:07:57.333 --> 00:07:58.333
Aah!

143
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.133
And Poké Puffs for Pikachu and the others.

144
00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.633
Huh? Where's Dedenne?

145
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.433
Denne!

146
00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.966
Ne, ne, ne, ne, ne, ne, ne.

147
00:08:11.033 --> 00:08:13.733
Denne!

148
00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.500
-Oh, no.

149
00:08:18.466 --> 00:08:19.733
Dedenne.

150
00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.733
Ne, ne, ne...

151
00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.833
Fennekin, Scratch.

152
00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.466
Fennekin!

153
00:08:26.533 --> 00:08:27.966
Kin, kin, kin, kin!

154
00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:29.600
Kin! Fenn?

155
00:08:29.666 --> 00:08:32.166
Dedenne! Oh! Denne-ne...

156
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.666
Dedenne's hurt. What do we do?

157
00:08:34.733 --> 00:08:36.700
Serena? Is there a Pokémon Centre?

158
00:08:36.766 --> 00:08:41.900
Hm. No. I don't see anything close by here.

159
00:08:41.966 --> 00:08:45.700
That's bad. We could really use Clemont's help right about now.

160
00:08:45.766 --> 00:08:49.166
Oh. Here. There's a clinic in the forest.

161
00:08:49.233 --> 00:08:50.700
Great. Come on.

162
00:08:50.766 --> 00:08:52.166
Pika!

163
00:08:52.233 --> 00:08:55.266
It's so quiet and peaceful here.

164
00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:58.033
It may be boring to someone from the city,

165
00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.233
but I really like living out here in nature.

166
00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:03.033
I really like it too.

167
00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.466
- Take a look.
- Huh?

168
00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:11.400
Would you look at that face?

169
00:09:11.466 --> 00:09:17.100
Wobbuffet seems so much happier here, leading a life filled with love.

170
00:09:17.166 --> 00:09:21.566
Huh? What about me? What would make me happier?

171
00:09:21.633 --> 00:09:24.466
I wonder, love or...

172
00:09:24.533 --> 00:09:28.133
- Something wrong?
- Uh... It's love.

173
00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.033
- Huh?
- No, no, no...

174
00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:34.033
Uh, I mean I love to look at them all. The Wobbuffet.

175
00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.066
Of course. Cute, aren't they?

176
00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:44.466
- An Ursaring.
- Don't worry. It's fine.

177
00:09:44.533 --> 00:09:46.266
See that? Oh?

178
00:09:46.333 --> 00:09:49.566
-That Ursaring was once a patient of mine.

179
00:09:51.666 --> 00:09:55.100
Hi, there. How've you been all this time?

180
00:09:55.166 --> 00:09:56.766
Say hello to Jessileah.

181
00:09:56.833 --> 00:09:59.433
She's been helping me out with all my medical work.

182
00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.366
Nice to meet you.

183
00:10:02.433 --> 00:10:06.033
I've decided. I choose love.

184
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.866
Who's that Pokémon?

185
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.866
It's Wynaut.

186
00:10:17.933 --> 00:10:19.666
Wynaut.

187
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:25.533
We know someone like Jessie wouldn't just vanish into thin air.

188
00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.700
Hey, what's that?

189
00:10:27.766 --> 00:10:31.500
Jessie? In those clothes?

190
00:10:31.566 --> 00:10:34.033
That's a weird get-up, even for her.

191
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.933
- Let's take a closer look.
- Righty-o.

192
00:10:39.066 --> 00:10:40.733
Excuse me.

193
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.666
Ugh! Twerps?

194
00:10:43.733 --> 00:10:47.200
Doctor, please help. Something happened to Dedenne and it's in trouble.

195
00:10:47.266 --> 00:10:50.300
Of course. Please come inside.

196
00:10:50.366 --> 00:10:52.933
Denne... ne-ne...

197
00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.733
I think it shocked itself when it got trapped inside a strange cage.

198
00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.266
Sounds like the work of that Pokémon hunter.

199
00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:01.500
- A Pokémon hunter?
- Pika?

200
00:11:01.566 --> 00:11:06.233
He's a bad guy who finds rare Pokémon and then sells them to make a profit.

201
00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.433
- Is Dedenne gonna be all right?
- Don't worry.

202
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:13.066
I'll drain off the excess electricity. It'll be fine.

203
00:11:13.133 --> 00:11:15.200
Eh... ne-ne...

204
00:11:15.266 --> 00:11:17.566
- Denne?
- Dedenne's fine.

205
00:11:17.633 --> 00:11:21.300
- Denne-ne!
- Dedenne! Thank you so much.

206
00:11:21.366 --> 00:11:25.066
Sure. A few Oran Berries will help Dedenne get its strength back.

207
00:11:25.133 --> 00:11:27.633
I'll go get some from the garden.

208
00:11:28.966 --> 00:11:30.500
Hm. Hm.

209
00:11:30.566 --> 00:11:32.433
- Good.
- Oh, awesome.

210
00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.666
- Wow. You sure have a lot of berries.
- There you go.

211
00:11:35.733 --> 00:11:37.400
- Thanks a lot.
- Denne!

212
00:11:37.466 --> 00:11:39.666
The doctor says he doesn't have enough.

213
00:11:39.733 --> 00:11:42.433
He hopes to grow every variety of berry that there is.

214
00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.900
Wobba, wob, wob, wob.

215
00:11:44.966 --> 00:11:47.733
Wait. There's something about that Wobbuffet...

216
00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.033
Heh, uh...

217
00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.366
I've never seen them before as a family.

218
00:11:51.433 --> 00:11:53.233
Over there. What's that?

219
00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:56.466
Uh, it's really nothing. Ugh!

220
00:11:56.533 --> 00:11:58.233
-It's you.

221
00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:01.733
Shh! Shh! My name is Jessileah.

222
00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.166
So that Wobbuffet is...

223
00:12:03.233 --> 00:12:04.433
I'm begging you!

224
00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.666
Please don't breathe a word about the fact that I'm in Team Rocket.

225
00:12:07.733 --> 00:12:09.400
- I'm grovelling.
- But why?

226
00:12:09.466 --> 00:12:11.533
I've decided I'm quitting Team Rocket,

227
00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:14.400
so I can live my life with Dr White forever.

228
00:12:16.533 --> 00:12:20.166
- Run that by me again?
- Jessie. No.

229
00:12:20.233 --> 00:12:23.466
Maybe Jess ate a bad berry. I'll go snap her out of it.

230
00:12:23.533 --> 00:12:24.866
- Stop.
- Ugh!

231
00:12:24.933 --> 00:12:26.666
Maybe she'll be better off.

232
00:12:26.733 --> 00:12:29.166
Did you eat a bad berry too?

233
00:12:29.233 --> 00:12:33.166
Listen, if Jessie's only trying to find a little happiness for herself,

234
00:12:33.233 --> 00:12:35.166
maybe we shouldn't stand in her way.

235
00:12:35.233 --> 00:12:39.533
After all, that's what real friends would do, wouldn't they?

236
00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.666
- Oh, James...
- Huh?

237
00:12:41.733 --> 00:12:44.666
Look. Wobbuffet's having a blast too.

238
00:12:44.733 --> 00:12:47.333
Yeah, I get it. See, I've been in love before.

239
00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.033
Believe you me, I have.

240
00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:52.166
And if Jessie and Wobbuffet wanna sail on that love boat...

241
00:12:52.233 --> 00:12:54.300
Let's not muddy the waters.

242
00:12:54.366 --> 00:12:55.633
We're outta here.

243
00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.166
- Kay.

244
00:12:57.233 --> 00:12:58.933
Jessie...

245
00:13:09.166 --> 00:13:12.000
I hope you find happiness. Goodbye.

246
00:13:14.333 --> 00:13:17.466
So does that mean you're gonna get married to the doctor?

247
00:13:17.533 --> 00:13:19.000
- Ah!
- Get married?

248
00:13:19.066 --> 00:13:22.600
That is what two people do when they decide they wanna be together.

249
00:13:22.666 --> 00:13:25.000
Wow. I guess that's really what it means.

250
00:13:26.733 --> 00:13:28.933
I think I'm going to get married.

251
00:13:30.566 --> 00:13:34.300
I just feel so lonely after saying goodbye to Jessie.

252
00:13:34.366 --> 00:13:37.966
Quit your whining. You'd better get used to the fact that from here on out,

253
00:13:38.033 --> 00:13:39.200
it's just going to be us.

254
00:13:39.266 --> 00:13:40.100
Kaboo?

255
00:13:40.166 --> 00:13:42.766
Looks like a run-of-the-mill trap to me.

256
00:13:42.833 --> 00:13:44.500
This must be the work of...

257
00:13:44.566 --> 00:13:45.833
That Pokémon hunter.

258
00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:47.533
In the flesh.

259
00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:52.033
Looks like I've found the greatest of all prey. A talking Meowth.

260
00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.766
You gotta do better than that.

261
00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:56.200
We're the new streamlined Team Rocket.

262
00:13:56.266 --> 00:13:58.266
- You bet.
- Pumpka.

263
00:13:58.333 --> 00:14:00.766
Let's go, Rhyperior.

264
00:14:02.533 --> 00:14:04.833
Rhy!

265
00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.566
Yeah. I'm gonna give it everything I've got.

266
00:14:07.633 --> 00:14:11.266
I'll show you how to tell the doctor everything you're feeling.

267
00:14:11.333 --> 00:14:14.400
That's so uncharacteristically nice of you, twerpette.

268
00:14:14.466 --> 00:14:15.933
- Doctor.
- Huh?

269
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.433
Is the doctor in?

270
00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.933
Yes!

271
00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.500
Aah!

272
00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:29.866
- What happened?
- You're a mess.

273
00:14:29.933 --> 00:14:32.666
Sorry, but would you mind helping me out?

274
00:14:32.733 --> 00:14:34.633
Huh? What happened?

275
00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.366
Meowth and all our Pokémon were stolen.

276
00:14:38.333 --> 00:14:41.300
We were attacked by a wily Pokémon hunter.

277
00:14:41.366 --> 00:14:44.600
Pokémon hunter? Dr White was talking about him.

278
00:14:44.666 --> 00:14:49.100
Just for today, I want to rescue Meowth without asking for help from Jessie.

279
00:14:49.166 --> 00:14:51.066
Then that must mean, you already...

280
00:14:51.133 --> 00:14:55.333
Yes. I know I'm asking a lot from you.

281
00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:57.833
But please, help me.

282
00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:01.633
If that guy's a Pokémon hunter, we can't just do nothing.

283
00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.500
- Thanks a lot.
- So where is he?

284
00:15:03.566 --> 00:15:06.633
At the foot of the mountain. I'll take you.

285
00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:13.800
A Pokémon hunter is holding Meowth, Inkay and Pumpkaboo captive.

286
00:15:13.866 --> 00:15:16.433
So what am I going to I do?

287
00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.133
Just what?

288
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.100
- Inkay. Inkay!
- Pumpkaboo!

289
00:15:21.166 --> 00:15:25.133
Will you take it easy, bub? We're Team Rocket, you dig?

290
00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.100
That big mouth of yours is quite a catch.

291
00:15:28.166 --> 00:15:29.766
Aw, how embarrassin'.

292
00:15:29.833 --> 00:15:32.666
Gettin' poached by a Pokémon comedian.

293
00:15:32.733 --> 00:15:34.933
You're gonna make me a fortune.

294
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.133
- Hold on.
- Huh?

295
00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.733
Who are you?

296
00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:41.266
You're a Pokémon hunter and you've gotta stop. Now!

297
00:15:41.333 --> 00:15:44.633
- Release the Pokémon you've stolen.
- We're not kidding.

298
00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:49.500
- So what are you twerps doing here?
- They're just a bunch of foolish kids.

299
00:15:49.566 --> 00:15:52.300
Let's go, Rhyperior.

300
00:15:52.366 --> 00:15:54.833
Rhy!

301
00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:57.266
- Who's that Pokémon?

302
00:15:58.566 --> 00:16:00.733
Rhyperior. The Drill Pokémon.

303
00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:04.566
Rhyperior launches rocks or Geodude from holes in its palms.

304
00:16:04.633 --> 00:16:09.400
Its shell-like covering can withstand a volcano's eruptions.

305
00:16:09.466 --> 00:16:13.400
- James! Yeah!
- Shh! Just a second.

306
00:16:13.466 --> 00:16:16.200
- Pikachu, Quick Attack.
- Pikachu!

307
00:16:16.266 --> 00:16:19.066
- Fennekin, Flamethrower.
- Fenn!

308
00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:22.700
Rock Wrecker, go.

309
00:16:22.866 --> 00:16:24.800
- Pika!
- Kin!

310
00:16:24.866 --> 00:16:27.300
- Rock Wrecker, again.
- Rhy!

311
00:16:29.733 --> 00:16:31.933
- What? Pokémon hunter?
- That's right. And...

312
00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.100
- Beatrice!
- Beatrice?

313
00:16:34.166 --> 00:16:36.866
- Beatrice. Ugh!
- What's wrong?

314
00:16:36.933 --> 00:16:39.733
- Why are you all worked up like that?
- All worked up?

315
00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.033
- I was worried about you, of course.
- About me?

316
00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:43.366
It's the Pokémon hunter.

317
00:16:43.433 --> 00:16:46.533
Knowing you, I thought you'd be in a big fight with him by now.

318
00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:51.233
- Hey. So you were worried about me.
- Of course I was worried!

319
00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.766
You're very important to me, so don't forget it.

320
00:16:55.833 --> 00:16:58.766
Wait a minute. Where did all this suddenly come from?

321
00:16:58.833 --> 00:17:02.866
OK. There's something I should have told you long ago...

322
00:17:02.933 --> 00:17:04.833
- Wobbuffet?
- Wob?

323
00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:08.733
- This is where we say goodbye.
- Wob. Wobba.

324
00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:12.233
You stay here and have a wonderful life.

325
00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.266
Wob!

326
00:17:18.333 --> 00:17:19.833
-Pika!

327
00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:26.133
- Piece of cake.
- Don't move a muscle, talking Meowth.

328
00:17:27.266 --> 00:17:31.333
I think it's time to teach you a lesson so you never try to escape again.

329
00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:32.933
What was that?

330
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.166
Prepare for trouble and that will be that

331
00:17:35.233 --> 00:17:37.233
And make it double or I'll knock you flat

332
00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.433
- I know that voice.
- And how.

333
00:17:41.933 --> 00:17:43.033
Jessie!

334
00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.500
To protect the world from devastation!

335
00:17:45.566 --> 00:17:46.666
Don't do it.

336
00:17:46.733 --> 00:17:49.000
To unite all people within our nation!

337
00:17:49.066 --> 00:17:52.466
But I thought you were gonna give up evildoin' for love.

338
00:17:52.533 --> 00:17:55.166
To denounce the evils of truth and love!

339
00:17:55.233 --> 00:17:58.466
- Jessie!
- Your turn.

340
00:17:58.533 --> 00:18:01.300
You've got it.

341
00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.033
To extend our reach to the stars above!

342
00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.266
- Jessie!
- And it's James.

343
00:18:07.333 --> 00:18:10.600
Team Rocket blasts off together at the speed of light!

344
00:18:10.666 --> 00:18:13.733
Surrender now or prepare for a unified fight!

345
00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.433
Meowth, that's right!

346
00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:16.700
- Pumpka!
- Inkay!

347
00:18:16.766 --> 00:18:20.166
- Huh? Where's Wobbuffet?
- Back there.

348
00:18:20.233 --> 00:18:23.633
A loving home life is what Wobbuffet seems to prefer now.

349
00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.266
So why don't we blast off at the speed of light?

350
00:18:26.333 --> 00:18:28.933
Right. And that is why they call us...

351
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.566
Team Rocket!

352
00:18:30.633 --> 00:18:32.633
OK. Use Horn Drill.

353
00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:35.000
Rhy!

354
00:18:42.533 --> 00:18:45.633
You're finished. Rock Wrecker.

355
00:18:48.666 --> 00:18:50.300
Wobbuffet!

356
00:18:50.366 --> 00:18:53.566
Wobbuff!

357
00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.766
- Rhyperior?
- Wobbuffet.

358
00:18:57.833 --> 00:19:03.200
Wobbuffet, you were so happy back there, so why did you come here? Go back now.

359
00:19:03.266 --> 00:19:05.333
Wob, wobba-wob.

360
00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:07.500
You left them for us?

361
00:19:07.566 --> 00:19:09.833
You're the best pally that ever was.

362
00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.833
You're a fool. A fool.

363
00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:14.833
OK. Fury Attack.

364
00:19:16.666 --> 00:19:19.133
OK. Go.

365
00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.766
- Us too.
- Pika.

366
00:19:22.033 --> 00:19:25.966
Wobbuffet!

367
00:19:28.033 --> 00:19:31.000
- Let's go.
- Wobba!

368
00:19:33.633 --> 00:19:36.633
- Now, Pumpkaboo, use Dark Pulse.
- Pumpka!

369
00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:40.033
- OK, Inkay, Psybeam.
- Inkay

370
00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:43.233
Pikachu, Thunderbolt. Pikachu!

371
00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:46.466
- Fennekin, Flamethrower.
- Fennekin!

372
00:19:58.733 --> 00:20:01.200
You really defeated the Pokémon hunter?

373
00:20:01.266 --> 00:20:04.100
It was all thanks to Jessileah.

374
00:20:04.166 --> 00:20:07.100
I'm sure Officer Jenny will be by soon.

375
00:20:07.166 --> 00:20:10.500
- Here. They're from Jessileah.
- Hm.

376
00:20:10.566 --> 00:20:14.333
- Wow, they're so beautiful.
- They are.

377
00:20:16.766 --> 00:20:19.633
I'll always be a member of Team Rocket.

378
00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:22.933
And I'll always have the greatest friends ever.

379
00:20:24.066 --> 00:20:26.933
With hearts united and overflowing with emotion,

380
00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.566
Team Rocket and their balloon fly on.

381
00:20:29.633 --> 00:20:32.133
Tomorrow will bring new adventures.

382
00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:37.433
I've finished inputting all of Ash's battle data. Ready?

383
00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.166
Cannot compute.

384
00:20:45.066 --> 00:20:47.600
As the journey continues.
